war in ukraine a chinese tech crackdown  and slipping stock prices pushed 329  people off forbes 2022 list of the  world's billionaires including 169  one-hit wonders who were part of last  year's record 493 newcomers it's the  largest number of drop-offs since 2009  when the financial crisis knocked 355  people off the list three countries  accounted for two-thirds of the  drop-offs china russia and the us china  had 153 drop-offs including four from  hong kong in fact of the 10 former  billionaires whose net worth sank the  most eight were from china the fortunes  of this year's two biggest losers jean  bangshin of tal education and larry  jiangdong chen of rival gsx tech edu  evaporated when the chinese government  took steps to ban profits and overseas  investment in the after-school tutoring  industry russia lost 35 billionaires  including oleg tinkov whose digital bank  tinkoff shed 90 of its share value in  london after russia invaded ukraine  before trading was suspended on march  2nd in late april tinkov announced he  would sell his remaining 35 stake in the  bank to billionaire oligarch vladimir  putin under pressure from the kremlin  after tinkov spoke out against the war  33 u.s billionaires fell off the list  including rj scarange founder and ceo of  startup electric vehicle maker rivian  less than a year ago rivien had raised a  record 23.1 billion dollars including  11.9 billion dollars in its november ipo  which valued the company at 90 billion  dollars but scarange has struggled to  ramp up production ever since  disappointing analysts and sending  shares spiraling 64 by forbes's march  11th measurement date for the list  former tech billionaires whose fortunes  soared more than any other group during  the pandemic were hit the hardest 53  dropped off including 32 from china and  hong kong  fashion and retail lost 45 billionaires  manufacturing lost 33 and real estate  lost 29. two of covet 19's biggest early  winners the healthcare and finance  sectors also lost 25 billionaires apiece
 

